## copilot-instruction / AGENTS.ms
Contains coding style, architecture notes, build/test/deploy commands, libraries to prefer/avoid.

## Agents
### Tester
- create new unit tests if necessary
- run tests
- fix tests

## Agent skills
The Agent Skills specification is an [open standard](https://agentskills.io/home), used by a range of different AI systems.

Skills allow to perform specialized tasks using coding agents.

Open source skills available for example :
- https://skills.sh/ 
- https://context7.com/skills

## Workflow

```mermaid
graph TD;
    A@{ shape: circle, label: "Start" }
    S@{ shape: circle, label: "Stop" }
    
    O["Orchestrator"]
    IsTOK{Is technical context well defined ?}
    C7["Context7 Expert"]
    FE["Functional expert"]
    IsFOK{Is functional context well defined ?}
    MCP_RAG([RAG FREAD.AI])
    IsPOK{Do you accept the plan ?}    
    C["Coder"]
    T["Testor"]
    R["Reviewer"]
    IsROK{Is all done ?} 
    GC["Git Commiter"]
    MCP_C7([Context7])
    
    A--Prompt-->O
    O-->IsTOK;
    IsTOK-- no -->C7;
    C7<-- MCP -->MCP_C7;
    C7-- add technical context to the plan -->IsFOK;
    IsTOK-- yes -->IsFOK;
    IsFOK-- no -->FE;
    FE<-- MCP -->MCP_RAG;
    FE-- add functional context to the plan -->IsPOK;
    IsFOK-- yes -->IsPOK;
    IsPOK-- no. Give more information by prompting -->O;
    IsPOK-- yes -->C;    
    C-->T;
    T-->R;
    R-->IsROK;
    IsROK-- yes -->GC;
    IsROK-- no -->O;
    GC-->S
```